-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Sep 03 18:39:57 UTC 2026 - Benjamin Zeller <bzeller@suse.de>

- plan_install/plan_remove and confirm_install/confirm_remove now
  select packages using the same algorithm as zypper (repository
  priority, vendor, architecture and version), instead of a
  simplified first-match lookup. A locked package is now reported as
  a solver conflict instead of having its lock silently cleared;
  removal no longer pulls in recommended packages; downgrades are now
  consistently allowed both while solving and during the actual
  commit.
- Fixed the packaged proxy binary looking for the worker in the wrong
  location, causing it to find no tools at all once installed.
- Added an installable QA testsuite package (mcp-server-zypp-
  testsuite) that exercises the installed server end to end over the
  real MCP protocol, covering GPG key trust, license confirmation,
  solver error reporting and commit failure diagnostics.
- version 0.1.2

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Aug 27 14:37:15 UTC 2026 - Benjamin Zeller <bzeller@suse.de>

- Tools are now split into root-gated confirm_install/confirm_remove
  (which commit changes) and plan_install/plan_remove plus read-only
  tools (which never require root); confirm_install/confirm_remove
  refuse to run without root privileges.
- GPG key trust decisions during confirm_install now go exclusively
  through interactive elicitation - no tool argument can pre-approve
  a key fingerprint, so an LLM agent can never silently bypass a
  package signature check.
- Added a license/EULA confirmation gate to confirm_install: an
  install that requires accepting a license is blocked until the
  license text has been explicitly accepted; re-accepting is skipped
  on upgrade only when the license text is provably unchanged.
- confirm_install/confirm_remove can now be cancelled cleanly while
  still solving or downloading packages; once the RPM transaction
  itself has begun it always runs to completion and is never
  interrupted.
- Progress notifications are now forwarded for package installation,
  removal and download, including systems where libzypp performs the
  transaction as a single rpm invocation (previously silently
  unsupported, falling back to a bare warning with no progress at
  all).
- confirm_install/confirm_remove now report detailed diagnostics when
  a commit fails, including which packages failed vs. were skipped
  and the underlying errors/warnings, instead of a single generic
  failure message. A failing RPM scriptlet no longer fails the whole
  operation silently; it is reported as a warning instead.
- Solver failure reports across all tools now include the full
  problem detail and proposed solutions, not just a one-line summary.
- Errors reported by tools are no longer summarized down to a short
  message; the full diagnostic detail is now preserved end to end.
- The HTTP transport is disabled by default until it has proper
  authentication; only the stdio transport is enabled out of the box.
- Fixed a potential crash when a tool call's JSON arguments were
  malformed or missing an expected field.
- version 0.1.1

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Aug 03 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - Benjamin Zeller <bzeller@suse.de>

- Initial package for mcp-server-zypp, an MCP server exposing
  libzypp package management operations to LLM agents via the
  Model Context Protocol.
- version 0.1.0
